{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/480202-infrastructure-examples","id":480202,"title":"Infrastructure Examples.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-14T07:23:03-07:00","id":480202,"title":"Infrastructure Examples.","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/480104-little-help-with-infrastructure-and-aether-production\">Mithrael's post</a> made me think: it'd be nice if we had a place for people to post their examples of Infrastructure.<br /> <br /> Infrastructure's one of those things that are essentially plot hooks for your game. Do you have any that you're proud of? Are they specific to your game, or can they be ported and use by others in different ways? Are they simple? Complex? Are they Command and Control? Defense? What do they provide when Suborned? What does a Demon have to do to use it if Suborned? What can happen when things go <i>wrong</i>?<br /> <br /> I'll give my own example, and hope to come up with more later.<br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <b>99.7 KFRC Oldies</b> (Command and Control)<br /> <br /> KFRC is a radio station that plays oldies. It only plays oldies. Its definition of oldies is the most traditional possible. But. Every Friday at 3:05 AM and 3:05PM, it plays a heavy metal song. Every caller that calls to complain about the heavy metal song is answered by the operator of the station, whose voice tends to sound just a little as if it were being parsed through autotune. It reassures the caller that the person responsible for the oversight will be handled, and asks for the caller's cellphone number.<br /> <br /> From then on, that caller will never be able to tune into 99.7 KFRC at 3:05 AM or 3:05 PM again, for a number of minutes equal to however long the heavy metal song playing lasts. Any radio or device that can catch radio waves within an audibly perceivable radius will be unable to tune into it. This effect is concentrated on their cellphone. If they change cellphones or don't have it near them, complications may arise.<br /> <br /> For every caller that calls to complaint, Aether is generated. For every person who attempts to tune into the station and cannot because they once called to complain, Aether is generated. Not only that, but the Infrastructure is slowly creating a pattern of people who check every Friday. Some are staying up late at night to wait for that moment in which they can't tune in. Some say they can hear something else in the static. Some even say they're hearing messages...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3855,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","user":"gebbethine","date":". 04-14-2015, 10:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T10:16:41-07:00","id":480390,"title":"","content":"<b>Waste processing plant</b><br /> <br /> In the run down side of the industrial part of town there is a plant that processes hazardous waste into safe materiel by 'cooking' it at extreme temperatures (real science thats I'm fuzzy on specifics). Those who work in this plant can be seen milling about for their shift, not once touching or doing anything just in constant movement often at different speeds. The whole plant is automized as the 'kiln' is filled with waste a green light turns on. At this point the linchpin of this infrastructure stirs. You see, there is no mechanism to power the kiln but rather an intentionally shaped cryptid that looks strikingly like a mechanical dragon (crocodile base, +1 size, alternate composition, blast (fire) numen, aether eater, aether hive). This beast is caged out of sight bellow the kiln and when it is ready to start it has been trained to react to the signal light. It must balance the energy it puts into its flames to what it will reap from its effort. The creature serves two purposes a) to run the kiln and b) the make it harder for unchained to find.<br /> <br /> The only question left is what is the purpose to the processed materiel? Does the plant do as advertised and even if it does are there unmentioned effects on this now 'safe' materiel that are never mentioned but somehow apart of the design.<br /> <br /> *Obviously not something they would just stumble on but I'd say players would find if they were trying to track something specific (potentially a waste materiel buried under new construction that is believed to be linked to a number of stigmatics creation?).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T08:00:29-07:00","id":481309,"title":"","content":"The Burning Bush (****)<br /> <br /> Durability 4, Size 2, Structure 4<br /> <br /> Description: This old Bush TR82 transistor portable radio is a classic of a bygone era. It doesn't have a scratch on it or a day's worth of wear and tear and always feels hot to the touch.<br /> <br /> Effect: Using the Burning Bush is simple. The user simply turns the dial on the front of the old transistor radio until they can find a station. This isn't as easy as it first seems as there is only ever one available station at any given time and the numbers that denote the station change frequently. Inevitably, however, after enough fiddling the user will tune in and hear their own voice speaking in a manner alike to the classic 'numbers stations' of the Cold War era. The voice will always speak in the language of the user and the numbers will eventually repeat for exactly 4 hours, 44 minutes and 4 seconds before returning to dead-air, even if the last of the message is incomplete.<br /> <br /> Decoding the message will always result in a foretelling of some future event, usually significant to the life of the user though sometimes significant to the world at large. The radio favours loud, dramatic or deeply unlikely events that the user is unlikely to believe until they happen and uses headlines and single phrases, forgoing in-depth details, to describe events. The Burning Bush never gives the user good news for very long, and each user only ever get 4 successful predictions before bad things start happening. Maybe their health starts to fail or accidents happen around them that see them injured, but eventually the whole world turns against the user as if reality itself is trying to kill an infection.<br /> <br /> The Burning Bush takes 1 Willpower to activate at which point the user receives their coded prophecy. The nature of the prophecy is at Storyteller discretion but it could be worth a +3 dice bonus, the removal of a surprise bonus in a later combat scene, or the knowledge of details like the combination to a safe. Decoding the prophecy is an Intelligence + Academics or Investigation roll and would benefit from a Mathematics or Coding speciality respectively.<br /> <br /> Each user may only gain 4 prophecies from the Burning Bush before its curse comes into effect. Each day the user will take 1 lethal damage, at any point, during the progress of the day. The Storyteller is encouraged to make bizarre and unlikely accidents and coincidences work together to cause the damage. This effect persists until the user throws the radio away, sells it or otherwise gets rid of the bygone from their life. (Simply passing ownership to another in the same household will not do.)<br /> <br /> The Burning Bush is not indestructible, but will fix itself over time. At the beginning of a new scene where the broken radio has been left alone for any length of time results in the radio being restored to perfect condition.<br /> <br /> Researching 'The Burning Bush'.<br /> <br /> Dice Pool: Intelligence + Academics<br /> Action: Extended \u2013 20 successes<br /> Research Time: (Standard) 1 hour per roll<br /> Possible Modifiers: Museum Library (+3), Tabloid and Urban Legend collection (+1)<br /> <br /> Successes Information<br /> 0-5 Nothing.<br /> 6-10 Tabloid and Conspiracy Journalist stories on the 'The Burning Bush' claim it was found in an archaeological dig in northern Iraq back in the 1923, 36 years before it's model would ever leave the assembly line in mass production.<br /> 11-15 A physical description or photograph of the actual radio along with a lengthy technical review of its internal workings and the fact that it only seems capable of receiving a clear signal from the constellation of Orion.<br /> 16-20 A detailed collection of reports on various 'prophecies' that the Radio has made throughout its time uncovered. Including the correct prediction of key historical events, from the outbreak of world wars, to the assassination of key political figures.<br /> <br /> Expanding on The Burning Bush<br /> <br /> As a simple bygone The Burning Bush can easily serve as the focus of a story but if the Storyteller or players want to pry into the workings of the radio itself and find out more about this seemingly ancient modern appliance, consider the following:<br /> <br /> Angelic Fetter: The Burning Bush may be the fetter or Infrastructure for an angel of the God-Machine. If this is the case, then it's likely the entity is a messenger of Rank 1 or 2 (and possibly very, very old.) It could have some unique numina that utilise the radio itself (examples below) and its ban and bane should be associated with the device (such as reciting previous predictions in their coded form back to the radio or an electro-magnet applied to the radio itself). Expanding on the radio in this way should replace the effect of the normal bygone.<br /> <br /> Coded Prophecy (Numen)<br /> The entity is able to tell a prophecy of coming events, usually dramatic or dangerous, via the object of its fetter or Reliant Condition (such as an anchor). The foretelling is always encoded in some way (be it in computer code, numerical code, pig latin or any other way of encrypting a message). The entity is only able to use this numen under certain conditions determined by their fetter and as a result this numen costs no essence.<br /> <br /> Murder by Improbability (Numen)<br /> Dice Pool: Power + Finesse \u2013 Presence + Supernatural Tolerance.<br /> Action: Instant<br /> Cost: 1 Essence<br /> The entity may cause fate to attack the target for them. If the entity succeeds in using this numen against a human being that is not possessed of some extraordinary fate (this is at Storyteller discretion, examples include: a world leader or player character of any kind) then they die within the next scene of some freak and bizarre accident.<br /> Characters with supernatural tolerance or some special fate instead suffer from all strikes against them during the next combat scene add the entity's rank to their rolls.<br /> <br /> Notes: The angel in this case likely attacks its victims with telekinesis to 'arrange the accidents' and to receive its dice bonus from Murder By Improbability. It would use its Influence to Strengthen the radio whenever it's damaged, restoring structure with essence. The angel's mission is likely, \u201cGive 4 prophecies and then kill.\u201d Any time it successfully completes this mission restore the health-levels of the killed target in essence (as per sacrifice).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T23:53:19-07:00","id":483236,"title":"","content":"The Clock Tower<br /> <br /> <br /> 23 years ago, the God-Machine started a plan involving creating a pocket reality. Considering its options, the least resource-consuming one would be harvesting the materials &quot;space-time&quot; to create it. <br /> <br /> The clocktower was created at a small town: everyday single day for the past 23 years and 10 months, at 2:31am, the clock &quot;steals&quot; 10 seconds from the city and all of its inhabitants. Stealing 10 seconds a day gives about 1 hours a year. in 24 years it will have stolen a whole day. When that happens, the God-Machine will have enough to go on with its plans, however, this disturbance is already creating physical tears in the reality: (lightning storms without clouds and etc. - Similar to an episode of Fringe if anyone has seen it).<br /> <br /> For those inside the city its like nothing happened: they resume whatever they were doing 10 seconds ago. Supposing someone was dropped a mug at 2:31:00, at 2:31:10 he would continue to see the mug falling. For those outside the city, and with unseen senses, at 2.31 they will hear the clocktower bell, and observe a distortion all around the city. (like when it see stuff by hot asphalt). Anyone who enters the city limits within this 10 seconds suffers the effects of the Clocktower.<br /> <br /> The only place &quot;safe&quot; of the effects is inside the tower itself (which also I believe should generate a huge amount of aether). The Tower is protected by a Guardian Angel who is always inside it during the 10 seconds. <br /> A la &quot;Back to the Future&quot; the Clocktower is only susceptible to electricity (which may become a huge problem for the Angel due to these unforeseen huge electrical storms starting to take place).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5690,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5690-mithrael","user":"Mithrael","date":". 04-17-2015, 03:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5690-mithrael","name":"Mithrael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5690_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}